// Regression fixture pinning the Task 7 review-fix behavior (memory-
// audit-4e whole-branch review, probe P4): a LOCAL container's element read
// escapes to a global. `p4Items[0]` is a list-INDEX read (`EIndexRef` at
// the IR level -- a raw `rt_list_at` borrow, never itself retained by
// cprint, unlike a MAP subscript's `IMapGet` intrinsic, which does retain
// internally -- see `lowStoreIntrOwnsResult`'s own doc comment for that
// distinction).
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores): `p4GSaved = p4Items[0]` is a
// NAMED-SLOT store (global) whose source is a non-birth element read --
// `lowCountedStore` retains it FIRST (confirmed against the emitted C:
// `rt_text_retain(cv___store1)` immediately after the `rt_list_at` borrow),
// THEN releases `p4GSaved`'s OLD (default-empty) handle.
//
// ARC Task 5 (counted container element slots) DELETED the old
// `lowEscapeContainerElemRisky`-gated "index-read disqualifies the
// container" consult that USED to be `p4Items`'s own disqualification
// reason -- but `p4Items` was ALSO always eligible for a real shallow
// release regardless (Task 4's unconditional local release), so that
// deletion changes `p4Items`'s DISPOSITION here, not its leak count:
// `p4Items` now qualifies for a DEEP release (confirmed against the
// emitted C: `{ int32_t i; for (...) rt_text_release(*(rt_text
// **)rt_list_at(cv_p4Items, i)); } rt_list_release(cv_p4Items);`, was a
// bare `rt_list_release` before) -- safe because the element it walks is
// `p4Items`'s OWN retained copy of the shared "ab" text (rc==2, from
// `p4GSaved`'s own retain above), so the walk's release only drops rc to 1,
// never to 0.
//
// `p4GSaved` itself stays globally-unqualified -- but for a DIFFERENT,
// UNRELATED rule than the one Task 5 deleted: `lowEscapeWalkAssign`'s own
// rule 4 (`p4GSaved = p4Items[0]`, a bare-identifier LHS reassigned from a
// rhs `lowEscapeFreshInit` doesn't recognize as fresh -- an `ExIndex` read
// is not one of that check's four fresh shapes, literal/concat/slice/[Task-
// 4-added, `lowStoreIsBirth`-only]call) -- this is Task 4's OWN pre-
// existing freshness test for DEEP-release/globals-qualification
// eligibility, entirely orthogonal to container-element counting, and
// untouched by Task 5. Confirmed against the emitted C: `cl_free_globals`
// stays empty (`p4GSaved` never appears in it). Expected strict-mode leak
// count: 2 (see ../p4_elem_escape.leaks, UNCHANGED by Task 5 -- the same
// total, now for a more precisely attributable reason) -- the shared
// `"a"+"b"` text's own remaining rc==1 (2 blocks), held solely by
// `p4GSaved`, itself never released (`cl_free_globals` stays empty for it
// -- Task 6's still-unmigrated globals-qualification scope, via rule 4's
// own non-fresh-reassignment test, not the deleted element-read consult).
// Not a bug -- globals-qualification is explicitly out of Task 5's scope.

var p4GSaved: text

func runP4ElemEscape() {
    var p4Items: list of text
    p4Items.push("a" + "b")
    p4GSaved = p4Items[0]
    alert("p4 done")
}
